  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#3381\", \"PowerToys#43082\", \"PowerToys#34238\"], \"answer\": \"Yes, this feature request has been filed before. Several tickets ask for PowerToys settings to sync across devices through an account sign-in. The main ticket is PowerToys#3381, and PowerToys#43082 was closed as a duplicate of PowerToys#34238. Built-in account sync does not exist yet. Until it does, use the Backup/Restore and import/export options in PowerToys Settings. Save the backup to OneDrive or another cloud folder, then restore it on your other PC. One commenter was unsure whether a backup can be restored on a different computer, because the backup file name may be tied to the machine it came from. You can also copy the settings JSON files from %LOCALAPPDATA%\\\\Microsoft\\\\PowerToys between PCs. Another option is a sync tool such as rclone. Add a thumbs-up to the existing tickets instead of opening a new one. Online editing and per-machine settings are not covered in those tickets, so you could add them there as extra requests.\"}",
